E('boudica|boudicca', 'Boudica was a queen of the Iceni tribe in Britain who led a revolt against Roman rule.', 'Her revolt took place around AD 60 or 61.', 'Romans had flogged her and seized her lands.', 'Her army burned Colchester, London and St Albans.', 'She was finally defeated by the Roman governor Suetonius.', 'A statue of her stands near the Houses of Parliament.')
E('hatshepsut', 'Hatshepsut was one of the few women to rule ancient Egypt as pharaoh.', 'She reigned from about 1479 to 1458 BC.', 'She was often shown with a false beard, as pharaohs traditionally were.', 'Her reign was peaceful and prosperous.', 'She sent a trading expedition to the land of Punt.', 'Later rulers tried to erase her from history.')
E('nefertiti', 'Nefertiti was a queen of ancient Egypt, wife of the pharaoh Akhenaten.', 'She lived in the 14th century BC.', 'Her painted bust in Berlin is one of the most famous artworks of the ancient world.', 'She and Akhenaten promoted worship of the sun disk, the Aten.', 'Her final fate is uncertain.')
E('akhenaten', 'Akhenaten was an Egyptian pharaoh who tried to change Egypt’s religion.', 'He ruled from about 1353 to 1336 BC.', 'He promoted worship of one god, the Aten, the sun disk.', 'He built a new capital at Amarna.', 'His changes were reversed after his death.', 'He was probably the father of Tutankhamun.')
E('wu zetian', 'Wu Zetian was the only woman to rule China as emperor in her own right.', 'She ruled from 690 to 705.', 'She rose from concubine to empress.', 'She expanded the civil service exams.', 'She supported Buddhism.', 'Traditional historians portrayed her harshly.')
E('eleanor of aquitaine', 'Eleanor of Aquitaine was one of the most powerful women of the Middle Ages.', 'She lived from about 1122 to 1204.', 'She was queen of France and then of England.', 'She went on the Second Crusade.', 'Two of her sons, Richard the Lionheart and John, became kings of England.')
E('queen isabella|isabella of castile|ferdinand and isabella', 'Isabella I of Castile and Ferdinand II of Aragon united Spain through their marriage.', 'Isabella lived from 1451 to 1504.', 'They completed the conquest of Granada in 1492.', 'They sponsored Columbus’s voyage the same year.', 'They expelled Jews from Spain in 1492.', 'They set up the Spanish Inquisition.')
E('mary queen of scots', 'Mary, Queen of Scots, ruled Scotland in the 16th century.', 'She lived from 1542 to 1587.', 'She became queen at six days old.', 'She was forced to abdicate in 1567 and fled to England.', 'Elizabeth I held her captive for 19 years.', 'She was executed in 1587 for plotting against Elizabeth.', 'Her son, James VI, later united the crowns of Scotland and England.')
E('eleanor roosevelt', 'Eleanor Roosevelt was an American First Lady, diplomat and activist.', 'She lived from 1884 to 1962.', 'She was married to Franklin D. Roosevelt.', 'She held her own press conferences and wrote a newspaper column.', 'She chaired the committee that drafted the Universal Declaration of Human Rights.')
E('indira gandhi', 'Indira Gandhi was India’s first and only female prime minister.', 'She lived from 1917 to 1984.', 'She was the daughter of Nehru.', 'She declared a state of Emergency from 1975 to 1977.', 'She was assassinated by her bodyguards in 1984.')
E('golda meir', 'Golda Meir was Prime Minister of Israel.', 'She lived from 1898 to 1978 and served from 1969 to 1974.', 'She grew up in the United States.', 'She was one of the world’s first female heads of government.', 'She led Israel during the Yom Kippur War in 1973.')
E('malala yousafzai|malala', 'Malala Yousafzai is a Pakistani activist for girls’ education.', 'She was born in 1997.', 'She was shot by the Taliban in 2012 for speaking out.', 'She survived and continued campaigning.', 'In 2014 she became the youngest Nobel Peace Prize laureate, at 17.')
E('mother teresa', 'Mother Teresa was a Catholic nun who cared for the poor in India.', 'She lived from 1910 to 1997.', 'She was born in what is now North Macedonia.', 'She founded the Missionaries of Charity in Kolkata in 1950.', 'She won the Nobel Peace Prize in 1979.', 'She was declared a saint in 2016.')
E('helen keller', 'Helen Keller was an American author and activist who was deaf and blind.', 'She lived from 1880 to 1968.', 'She lost her sight and hearing after an illness as a baby.', 'Her teacher, Anne Sullivan, taught her to communicate.', 'She was the first deafblind person to earn a bachelor’s degree.', 'She campaigned for disability rights and women’s suffrage.')
E('sacagawea', 'Sacagawea was a Lemhi Shoshone woman who helped the Lewis and Clark expedition.', 'She lived from about 1788 to 1812.', 'She served as interpreter and guide.', 'She travelled with her baby son.', 'Her presence signalled to other nations that the expedition was peaceful.')
E('pocahontas', 'Pocahontas was a Powhatan woman linked to the early English colony at Jamestown.', 'She lived from about 1596 to 1617.', 'The story that she saved John Smith may be exaggerated.', 'She married the colonist John Rolfe.', 'She travelled to England, where she died.')
E('spartacus', 'Spartacus was a gladiator who led a major slave revolt against Rome.', 'The revolt lasted from 73 to 71 BC.', 'He escaped from a gladiator school in Capua.', 'His army grew to perhaps 70,000 or more.', 'He defeated several Roman armies.', 'He was killed in battle, and 6,000 captured rebels were crucified along the Appian Way.')
E('hannibal elephants', 'Hannibal took war elephants across the Alps to invade Italy.', 'He crossed in 218 BC.', 'He started with around 37 elephants.', 'Most died in the cold or in the following months.', 'He still won huge victories in Italy.')
E('genghis khan descendants|timur|tamerlane', 'Timur, known in the West as Tamerlane, was a Turco-Mongol conqueror.', 'He lived from 1336 to 1405.', 'He built an empire across Central Asia, Persia and beyond.', 'His capital was Samarkand.', 'His campaigns were extremely brutal.', 'His descendant Babur founded the Mughal Empire.')
E('vlad the impaler|dracula', 'Vlad III, known as Vlad the Impaler, was a prince of Wallachia, in modern Romania.', 'He lived from about 1431 to 1476.', 'He was famous for impaling his enemies.', 'He fought the Ottoman Empire.', 'His family name, Dracula, inspired Bram Stoker’s vampire novel of 1897.')
E('blackbeard|pirates|golden age of piracy', 'Blackbeard was one of the most famous pirates of the Golden Age of Piracy.', 'He died in 1718; the golden age lasted roughly from 1650 to 1730.', 'His real name was probably Edward Teach.', 'He reportedly tied lit fuses in his beard to scare enemies.', 'He blockaded Charleston harbour in 1718.', 'He was killed in battle by the Royal Navy.')
E('nostradamus', 'Nostradamus was a French astrologer famous for prophecies.', 'He lived from 1503 to 1566.', 'He published Les Prophéties in 1555.', 'His verses are vague enough to be matched to many events.', 'He was also a physician who treated plague victims.')
